# Xbox Scarlett executable import analysis

The analyzed image is the x64 `game_scarlett_master.exe` from the Scarlett package labeled 1.0.2.1. Both examined copies had SHA-256 `E95020B2FA4A721DB3DF59FDECF75621730AC559D8835252F6C3B658D5A08993`.

## Findings

- The executable has 587 direct imports across 68 import descriptors. Of those, 341 resolved against Windows exports, 209 matched bundled exports, and 37 depended on seven unavailable Xbox DLLs.
- The unresolved modules are `xmem.dll`, `d3d12_xs.dll`, `chad.dll`, `xg_xs.dll`, `XCRDAPI.dll`, `xapu.dll`, and `AcpHal.dll`.
- Both Windows Sandbox debug runs armed the entry breakpoint at RVA `0x056A1EC8`. The loader exited with `0xC0000135` before hitting it. Both loader traces reported failures for `xmem.dll` and `twinapi.appcore.dll`. The startup trace reported a failure for `MSVCP140.dll` only in the mapped-folder run.
- The CodeView record names `game_scarlett_master.pdb`, GUID `2a6912ba-eb4f-427f-4c4c-44205044422e`, age 1. A matching PDB was unavailable. The PE inventory records the `__XMemAllocationHooks__` export and 299,257 x64 unwind records.

## Data

| File | Contents |
| --- | --- |
| [PE inventory](Xbox-GDK-PE-inventory.json) | Sections, debug metadata, imports, exports, and selected call-site candidates for the executable and 16 DLLs |
| [Import audit](Xbox-GDK-import-audit.json) | Import-level resolution by DLL, name or ordinal, and IAT RVA |
